  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Stonex Financial obligated $970M in FY26 to date across 297 awards, with an average award size of $3.3M. Stonex Financial obligations fell 27.1% year over year. Stonex Financial saw larger prior-year totals, including $1.3B in FY25 and $703M in FY24, and earlier peaks of $1.7B in FY22 and FY23. Stonex Financial has a multi-year presence in federal contracting, with FY21 obligations at $1.1B and a current-year total that is a partial fiscal-year figure. Stonex Financial award activity shows a mix of award count and dollar concentration, with the award count at 297 indicating many individual buy actions while the average award size of $3.3M indicates mid-sized awards on a per-award basis. Stonex Financial year-over-year movement and the fiscal-year series provide a quick view of how obligations have changed across FY21 to FY26.",
